---
name: flaky-test-qa-assignment
version: 2.1.0
description: Render a fenced-JSON assignment for flaky-test-qa in atm-bd-orchestration. `sprint_doc` is the file quality-mgr writes by piping `bd show <checked bead> --json` (the bead is the sprint plan); `carry_forward_findings_json` is a JSON array of the reviewer's own finding ids (`metadata.finding_ref` of the carried finding beads). Triage records are replaced by finding beads and are always empty.
format: json
required_variables:
  - worktree_path
  - branch
  - commit
  - review_targets
defaults:
  phase: ""
  sprint: ""
  round_limit: false
  changed_files: []
  carry_forward_findings_json: "[]"
  notes: ""
---
{%- set cf = carry_forward_findings_json | replace(" ", "") -%}
{%- set locked = cf not in ["", "[]", "null", "[null]", "[\"\"]"] -%}
{%- set rule = "FLAKY-TEST RULE (mandatory in every repository): flaky tests are prohibited by design. A test that relies on a race, timing, sleep, wall-clock deadline or assertion, poll-until-timeout, event-loop ordering or host load, and any wait that can block forever, is a blocking finding whatever its severity. Its remedy redesigns the test to be deterministic with controlled inputs: an injected clock or fake timers, or an explicit handshake (channel, notify, fifo, readiness signal). A failure-only hang deadline is allowed only as a backstop that fails with captured output, never as the synchronization. A passing run, even repeated under load, is not evidence that no race exists." -%}
{
  "worktree_path": {{ worktree_path }},
  "branch": {{ branch }},
  "commit": {{ commit }},
  "scope": {
    "phase": {% if phase %}{{ phase }}{% else %}null{% endif %},
    "sprint": {% if sprint %}{{ sprint }}{% else %}null{% endif %}
  },
  "review_targets": [{% for target in review_targets %}{{ target }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}],
  "round_limit": {% if round_limit %}true{% else %}false{% endif %},
  "changed_files": [{% for file in changed_files %}{{ file }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}],
  "triage_records": [],
  "carry_forward_findings": {{ carry_forward_findings_json | safe }},
  "notes": {{ ((rule ~ " " ~ notes) if notes else rule) ~ (" SCOPE LOCK: this is a fix-round verification dispatch. Report a disposition (fixed | open | regressed) for each id in carry_forward_findings ONLY. Do not add any new finding to the `findings` array beyond those ids, even if you notice something real and unrelated -- put anything else observed under `notes`, not `findings`." if locked else "") }}
}
